<%#
  Shows a whole email (its own <html>, <head>, <style>) inside the page without letting anything in
  it run. Local: html — the email's HTML as a String.

  Why a frame and not sanitize: the email body contains text other people wrote (a custom
  notification body, record names). Printed raw into the page, a `<img onerror=…>` in it ran as
  script for whoever opened it, including the LP recipient on the notification page
  (docs/security/security_coverage_gaps_2026_11.md). Sanitizing would also strip the email's
  <style>, so the preview would stop looking like the email.

  How it stays safe and looks the same:
    * srcdoc       — the email is its own document: its CSS can't leak into the app, the app's
                     CSS can't leak into it (the preview shows what the recipient sees)
    * sandbox      — no allow-scripts, so no script in the email ever runs; no allow-forms either.
                     allow-same-origin only lets the script below read the email's height
    * allow-popups + <base target="_blank"> — links in the email open in a new tab
    * the nonce'd script sizes the frame to the email, so the page reads like before (no inner
      scrollbar). It uses the CSP nonce, not an inline handler, and needs no app JavaScript
      (the preview page is rendered without the app's layout).
%>
<% frame_id = "sandboxed_email_#{SecureRandom.hex(6)}" %>
<iframe id="<%= frame_id %>" title="Email content"
        sandbox="allow-same-origin allow-popups allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox"
        srcdoc="<%= "<base target=\"_blank\">#{html}" %>"
        style="display: block; width: 100%; min-height: 120px; border: 0;"></iframe>
<%= javascript_tag nonce: true do %>
  (function () {
    var frame = document.getElementById("<%= frame_id %>");
    if (!frame) return;
    // Step 1: grow the frame to the email's full height once it has laid out
    function fit() {
      var doc = frame.contentDocument;
      if (doc && doc.documentElement) frame.style.height = doc.documentElement.scrollHeight + "px";
    }
    // Step 2: fit on load (and right away if it already loaded before this ran)
    frame.addEventListener("load", fit);
    if (frame.contentDocument && frame.contentDocument.readyState === "complete") fit();
  })();
<% end %>
